   "short": false,
   "hook": "Hangul Day turns 100",
   "name_chips": true,
   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Last story, a softer one. Last Friday, October ninth, was Hangul Day. Our historian, Dr. H.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_073.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Last time, I told you who made Hangul. This time, the holiday itself has a birthday. It turned one hundred.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_074.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "y100"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "The holiday is a hundred? Who threw the first party?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_075.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "In nineteen twenty-six, the Korean Language Society held the first celebration, for the four hundred eightieth anniversary of the fourteen forty-six text.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_076.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "haerye",
      "t1926"
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "What was it called?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_077.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "\"Gagya Day.\" It comes from the opening syllables of the Korean alphabet chart: ga, gya, geo, gyeo.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_078.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "gagya"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So it was literally Alphabet Day. Like \"A-B-C Day.\"",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_079.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "Two years later, in nineteen twenty-eight, it was renamed Hangul Day. And the date moved several times before it settled on October ninth.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_080.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "It lost its day off in the early nineties. In the mid-two-thousands it became an official national day again, but still without a day off. The day off came back in twenty thirteen.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_081.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "tstatus"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "A holiday that got laid off and rehired.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_082.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Why is it in the news? Because of foreign learners. This week, the King Sejong Institute Foundation invited a record three hundred fifty-seven Korean learners to Korea.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_083.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "sejong_poster",
      "n357"
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "A hundred eighty-one of them came to a speaking and writing contest, from seventy-one countries.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_084.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "n181"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Seventy-one countries. That's more than I've visited, even in my head.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_085.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The speaking contest had about two hundred eighty-four applicants for every finalist spot.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_086.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "speech",
      "ratio"
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "That's harder than getting concert tickets.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_087.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "The grand prize in speaking went to Marjan Haghi of Iran. In writing, it went to Nguyen Bao Chau of Vietnam.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_088.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "award_group"
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "The writing finalists wrote their essays wearing Joseon-era scholar robes.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_089.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "scholar"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Finally, a dress code for homework.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_090.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Why do they learn Korean? A King Sejong Institute survey found \"Korean content, such as K-pop, dramas, and movies\" was the top reason, at fifty-three point four percent. It was the first time that answer ranked number one.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_091.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "pct534"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So the idol songs were homework in disguise.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_092.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "One learner from Cairo, Amira Kamal Mohamed, started with the K-pop group EXO. She has studied Korean for ten years. She said it feels like she's inside a K-drama.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_093.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "A learner from Canada, who started with K-pop in twenty nineteen, said that being able to read it makes her feel her Korean has really improved.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_094.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      2560,
      470,
      1.3
     ],
     "ease": 0.12,
     "cam_id": "guest",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Reading is the real level-up. The first time I read a menu, I felt like I'd won a trophy.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_095.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "And it's not only fandom. A foundation survey in twenty twenty-five found fifty point nine percent of foreign learners were preparing to study in Korea. Thirty-seven percent cited career goals.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_096.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_anchor",
     "push": false,
     "screen": "study"
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "So it's not just a crush. It's a plan.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_097.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "guest",
     "text": "And that's the point of Hangul. King Sejong wanted ordinary people to read and write. Five hundred eighty years later, they're still learning it, sometimes from a song.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_098.mp3",
     "shot": "k_screen",
     "cam_id": "screen_guest",
     "push": false,
     "screen": [
      "statue",
      "night"
     ]
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "Let's wrap up. Hackers, a hypersonic test, and an alphabet.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_099.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "Core, what's your take?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_100.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "My take: AI is making attacks faster. So the best defense is slow. Hang up, then call your bank yourself.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_101.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And the missile?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_102.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "I'll leave that one to Ms. Nonfic. She doesn't have opinions.",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_103.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "text": "And the alphabet?",
     "audio": "audio/v1/ep06_104.mp3",
     "shot": "cam",
     "cam": [
      960,
      500,
      1.1
     ],
     "ease": 0.14,
     "cam_id": "two",
     "push": false
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "text": "The alphabet wins. One hundred years of a holiday, and people are still learning it. Thanks for watching.",
